From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SacredTrees <121399723+SacredTrees@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 16:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fold-mem-offsets: a memory-to-memory move is no root

fold-mem-offsets folds a constant add into the memory accesses that use
its result and then deletes the add, once every use of the result is a
"root": an instruction get_fold_mem_root() takes as a load or store it
can change.  An instruction with a MEM on both sides, which m68k has
(move.b (a1),2(a0)), was taken as a root for its source's address only.
The add feeding the destination's base register then had all its uses
marked as roots, was deleted, and the destination kept its old
displacement.

GFOpenBench's PREFSWB_judge.c stored four bytes through
p = out + here + 8; at -O2 with -m68040 or -m68060 the one whose source
was memory came out as move.b (a1),2(a0) where 10(a0) is right, so a
Workbench prefs chunk id was written "WB\0C" (gfopenbench #216).

get_fold_mem_root() now refuses an instruction whose destination is a
MEM and whose source is a MEM or a sign or zero extend of one.  Neither
address is folded into such an instruction, and an add that feeds one
stays.  On m68k the pass found almost nothing else to fold, and
-fno-fold-mem-offsets, which turns it off, removed the fault alone.

tests/repro/fmo.c is the case cut down (Team 5's trace); prove.sh runs it
at -O2 and -O3 with -m68040 and -m68060, and -Os.

Team 2 (Lister)
---
 gcc/fold-mem-offsets.cc | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/gcc/fold-mem-offsets.cc b/gcc/fold-mem-offsets.cc
--- a/gcc/fold-mem-offsets.cc
+++ b/gcc/fold-mem-offsets.cc
@@ -596,6 +596,18 @@
 	  || GET_CODE (dest) == UNSPEC_VOLATILE)
 	return false;
 
+      /* A memory-to-memory move (m68k's move.b (a1),2(a0)) has two
+	 addresses.  This pass changes only the one MEM it returns, and a
+	 definition is folded once every use is a root, so an add feeding
+	 the other address would be deleted with that address left as it
+	 was.  Such an instruction is no root.  */
+      if (MEM_P (dest)
+	  && (MEM_P (src)
+	      || ((GET_CODE (src) == SIGN_EXTEND
+		   || GET_CODE (src) == ZERO_EXTEND)
+		  && MEM_P (XEXP (src, 0)))))
+	return false;
+
       if (MEM_P (src))
 	mem = src;
       else if (MEM_P (dest))
